    {
      "title": "Welcome to the Dendron go-to-work Fork",
      "description": "# Welcome, Developer!\n\nYou are about to take the **primary onboarding CodeTour** for the Dendron personal maintenance fork (\"go-to-work\").\n\nDendron is a local-first hierarchical markdown note-taking system that feels like an IDE for your brain. This fork exists to keep it alive and working on 2025-2026 Node + VS Code.\n\n**This tour will:**\n- Get your environment ready\n- Teach you the mental model\n- Show you the most important files and commands\n- Point you at deeper tours for debugging, architecture, each package, etc.\n\n**How to navigate this tour:**\n- Use the **CodeTour** tree view in Explorer sidebar (or status bar)\n- Keyboard: `Cmd+Right` / `Cmd+Left` (or Ctrl on Windows/Linux)\n- The floating comment UI at the bottom of the editor has Previous/Next/End\n\n> **Pro tip**: Keep the CodeTour sidebar visible while taking tours. It is often faster than the inline UI.\n\nWhen you're ready, click **Next** (or press the keyboard shortcut).",
      "commands": ["workbench.view.explorer"]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Most Important Document: FORK-README.md",
      "description": "This file explains **why this fork exists**, the current branch strategy, immediate goals, and the modernized quick-start commands.\n\nRead it now (it is short and high-signal).\n\n[Open full FORK-README.md](./FORK-README.md)\n\nKey points you will learn:\n- The `codetour` branch (where these tours live)\n- `go-to-work` is the active dev branch\n- Recommended: open `dendron-plugin.code-workspace` instead of the raw folder\n- The entire `docs/dev/` series (this tour will take you there)\n\n>> cat FORK-README.md | head -60\n\n(Click the shell command above to run it in a dedicated CodeTour terminal.)",
      "file": "FORK-README.md",
      "line": 1,
