    {
      "title": "Directory Step: The docs/dev/packages/ Breakdowns",
      "description": "Every major package has a dedicated `.md` file here written by the fork maintainer.\n\nThese are **gold**. Read them alongside the per-package CodeTours you will find under `.tours/packages/`.\n\nExample files:\n- `plugin-core.md` (the heart of the VS Code extension)\n- `engine-server.md`\n- `common-all.md` (the type foundation everything imports)\n\nClicking **Next** will take you to the root README and the actual source layout.",
      "directory": "docs/dev/packages"
    },
    {
      "title": "Root package.json - The Monorepo Contract",
      "description": "This is a **Yarn workspaces + Lerna + custom bootstrap** monorepo (with Turbo for some caching).\n\nKey things to look for in this file:\n- `workspaces.packages`\n- `scripts` (especially `bootstrap:*`, `gen:data`)\n- `resolutions` (the horror that keeps old deps working)\n- `engines` (Node version expectations)\n\nWe will use shell commands and task commands heavily in later steps.\n\n[Open root package.json](./package.json)\n\n>> yarn --version && node --version\n\n(Shell commands prefixed with `>>` become clickable and run in a special \"CodeTour\" integrated terminal.)",
      "file": "package.json",
