    {
      "title": "Your First Real Command: bootstrap:build:fast",
      "description": "## The Daily Driver Build Command\n\nAfter a fresh clone or branch switch, run:\n\n```bash\nyarn bootstrap:build:fast\n```\n\nThis builds the common packages + engine-server + plugin-core (the minimum needed to F5 the extension).\n\n**In this tour we will not actually run the long build** (it can take 30-90s), but you should run it in your real terminal after this tour.\n\nInstead, here is a **lighter smoke task** you can run right now via a CodeTour command link:\n\n[Run doctor:smoke task](command:workbench.action.tasks.runTask?[\"doctor:smoke (health --verbose + json)\"])\n\nWatch the terminal output — it exercises the CLI + engine health checks.",
      "file": "package.json",
      "line": 20,
      "pattern": "bootstrap:build:fast"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Heart: packages/plugin-core/src/extension.ts + _extension.ts",
      "description": "All VS Code extensions start at `activate()`. Dendron immediately delegates (the `_` prefix is a deliberate signal that the real implementation lives in the sibling file).\n\n**Critical files you will set breakpoints in constantly:**\n- `packages/plugin-core/src/extension.ts` (the public surface)\n- `packages/plugin-core/src/_extension.ts` (the 700+ line monster that does DI, telemetry, WorkspaceActivator, command registration...)\n\n[Open extension.ts](./packages/plugin-core/src/extension.ts)\n\n[#7] (jump to the next step in this tour which highlights the delegation)\n\nSee also the full deep dive tour: [Extension Activation Lifecycle Tour][2: Extension Activation Lifecycle]",
      "file": "packages/plugin-core/src/extension.ts",
      "line": 5,
      "selection": {
        "start": { "line": 1, "character": 1 },
        "end": { "line": 17, "character": 1 }
