      "title": "Next Steps After This Tour (The Full Learning Path)",
      "description": "## Your Personalized Learning Path\n\n1. **Architecture & Mental Model** (next tour in this series)\n2. **Debugging Dendron with Breakpoints** (the most practical tour)\n3. **Build System Deep Dive**\n4. **Extension Activation Lifecycle** (the single most important flow)\n5. Pick a package tour from `.tours/packages/`\n\nAll of these tours deliberately cross-link using CodeTour's tour reference syntax so you can jump around.\n\n**After the tours**, read the full `docs/dev/` series in order.\n\nYou now have everything you need to be productive.\n\n---\n\n**End of primary onboarding tour.**\n\nThank you for taking the time. The `codetour` branch and these tours exist precisely so that Dendron's incredible engineering (and the fork's modernization work) is not lost.\n\n**Latest achieved state (post-merge from main)**: 0 strict production src/, DI 100% GREEN (v2 `inject()` helper + 0 bare decorators), doctor 6+table LIVE with full smoke ownership, extraction PR #1 landed (common-di phase 2 + ErrorService foundation), Lerna A+B recommendations, final Clean Host debug launch smoke green.\n\n[Return to CodeTour view](command:codetour.focusToursView)\n\n[Open the full .tours/README.md](./.tours/README.md)",
